{"id": "EUVD-2026-55585", "enisaUuid": "c65ae483-0db9-36cb-b293-381f20fd57d4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix UAF in sock clone early bailouts\n\nSimilar to recent commit 9b51a6155d14 (\"bpf,fork: wipe ->bpf_storage\nbefore bailouts that access it\"), sk_clone() performs an initial\nshallow copy of the socket field ->sk_bpf_storage via sock_copy()\nfor the cloned socket newsk.\n\nIf sk_clone() bails out early (e.g. if sk_filter_charge() fails) prior\nto calling bpf_sk_storage_clone(), newsk->sk_bpf_storage still points\nto the parent socket's BPF local storage. When newsk is subsequently\nfreed via sk_free(), the deallocation path (__sk_destruct() ->\nbpf_sk_storage_free()) destroys the parent socket's BPF local storage,\nleading to a use-after-free (UAF) on the parent socket.\n\nFix this by resetting newsk->sk_bpf_storage to NULL immediately after\nsock_copy() in sk_clone(), and remove the now redundant initialization\nfrom bpf_sk_storage_clone().", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:04:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:57", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f6814814b3bdd6ecb6bc1fc53ba4e827e0185f01", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24139461545e44442df9b80deace26b2eb3e103d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01f8a354497ba739f81b691b3702bc4c46500a4d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14b49b5ab29979552c219a09e569b424fbbf4a6e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7cbd0c4cebe4c9f678d15e6b9ba975e1155a107f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-68399", "GHSA-f9jq-9v6w-22v9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "35983bcd-0684-3f32-a1d4-75d41794fe86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "5d362c3b-95aa-36f7-ac36-8c5b6bf5d6c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "7a8d62a3-5424-3f49-9f22-54597ac524a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "817f40eb-65e9-332f-a438-ce1523459f1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6ac99e8f23d4b10258406ca0dd7bffca5f31da9d <01f8a354497ba739f81b691b3702bc4c46500a4d"}, {"id": "929b1471-77b4-315a-b519-c7f18b47a0ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6ac99e8f23d4b10258406ca0dd7bffca5f31da9d <f6814814b3bdd6ecb6bc1fc53ba4e827e0185f01"}, {"id": "971e0e9c-1ecd-39ad-b479-cbedc6460710", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b13ed84b-bbf5-3a6e-9c17-070c042b5a98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6ac99e8f23d4b10258406ca0dd7bffca5f31da9d <24139461545e44442df9b80deace26b2eb3e103d"}, {"id": "bd49a5d5-94f3-37aa-bf25-a0de4adce263", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6ac99e8f23d4b10258406ca0dd7bffca5f31da9d <7cbd0c4cebe4c9f678d15e6b9ba975e1155a107f"}, {"id": "c2e70565-5ab5-331f-a59b-c3a2651cf704", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "d66af4dc-ba21-3d29-a8cc-d526e337f58d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6ac99e8f23d4b10258406ca0dd7bffca5f31da9d <14b49b5ab29979552c219a09e569b424fbbf4a6e"}, {"id": "e427a48e-d8ef-38e2-a536-ad52902e0be2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "f818045e-d7f3-3fdf-8224-a0470e95dcf8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b3ddc83f-9b43-3a5f-9b83-80267de65111", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}